<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="System Design" id="system-design">
    <mxGraphModel>
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="2" value="Design a Distributed Job Scheduler" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="600" height="40" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3" value="Functional Requirements" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#f5f5f5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="80" width="420" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="4" value="1. Support scheduling recurring and one-time jobs&#10;2. Execute jobs on worker machines (Docker images, client-built; workers pull)&#10;3. Support status tracking of scheduled jobs&#10;4. Support retries for failed jobs (configurable per job)&#10;5. Support observability into each execution attempt&#10;6. Allow cancel / alter of jobs before they have run&#10;7. At-least-once execution&#10;&#10;Out of scope: workflow engine (DAGs, checkpointing, recovery)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="110" width="520" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5" value="Non-Functional Requirements" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#f5f5f5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="300" width="420" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="6" value="Latency: &lt; 3s between scheduled time and execution start&#10;Durability: required for accepted jobs&#10;Availability: 99.99% on submission API; status path eventually consistent&#10;&#10;Scale:&#10;  - Submission: 1k/s steady, 10k/s peak (immediate one-offs)&#10;  - Dispatch: 10k/s peak&#10;  - Concurrent executions: 10k&#10;  - DB writes: up to 10k/s&#10;&#10;Storage:&#10;  - Active pending jobs: ~3.6M rows (1k/s × 1h avg lead time)&#10;  - Execution attempts: 7 days hot, then S3 cold" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="330" width="520" height="240" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7" value="Core Entities" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#f5f5f5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="80" width="420" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8" value="Job&#10;  id&#10;  dockerImageUrl&#10;  createdAt&#10;  scheduledAt&#10;  status: scheduled | running | cancelled&#10;  retryConfig" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="110" width="420" height="130" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9" value="JobExecutionAttempt&#10;  id&#10;  jobId&#10;  attemptNumber&#10;  logs&#10;  error&#10;  status&#10;  createdAt" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="250" width="420" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10" value="ChronSchedule&#10;  id&#10;  cron_details" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="400" width="420" height="80" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="11" value="RecurringJob&#10;  id&#10;  dockerImageUrl&#10;  createdAt&#10;  chronScheduleId&#10;  retryConfig&#10;&#10;Note: each valid recurrence is materialized as a Job row" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="490" width="420" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="12" value="API Design (auth: JWT)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#f5f5f5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="600" width="980" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="13" value="1. POST /jobs  (Idempotency-Key header)&#10;     body: { scheduledAt, dockerImageUrl, retryConfig }&#10;     -&gt; { id }&#10;&#10;2. POST /recurringJobs  (Idempotency-Key header)&#10;     body: { chronScheduleId, dockerImageUrl, retryConfig }&#10;     -&gt; { id }&#10;&#10;3. GET /jobs/:id&#10;     -&gt; { id, status, scheduledAt, createdAt, dockerImageUrl, retryConfig }&#10;&#10;4. GET /jobs/:id/attempts&#10;     -&gt; [ { id, jobId, attemptNumber, status, logs, error, createdAt } ]&#10;&#10;5. GET /recurringJobs/:id&#10;     -&gt; { id, chronScheduleId, dockerImageUrl, retryConfig, createdAt }&#10;&#10;6. GET /recurringJobs/:id/instances&#10;     -&gt; [ Job rows: { id, status, scheduledAt, createdAt } ]&#10;&#10;7. DELETE /jobs/:id          (cancel before run; 409 if already running/completed)&#10;&#10;8. PATCH /jobs/:id&#10;     body: { scheduledAt }&#10;&#10;9. DELETE /recurringJobs/:id  (cancel before run; 409 if already running)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="630" width="980" height="450" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="20" value="High-Level Architecture" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#f5f5f5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1100" width="1380" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_client" value="Internal&#10;Services&#10;(Clients)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1170" width="120" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_lb" value="Load Balancer" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="220" y="1170" width="120" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_jobsvc" value="Job Service&#10;(API)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="1170" width="140" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_db" value="DB&#10;Job / RecurringJob / ChronSchedule / JobExecutionAttempt&#10;Index: (scheduledAt, status)&#10;Hash-partitioned on job_id" style="shape=cylinder3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=15;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="600" y="1170" width="280" height="120" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_sqs" value="SQS Queue" style="shape=mxgraph.aws4.queue;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="940" y="1180" width="120" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_workers" value="Worker Pool&#10;(consumes SQS;&#10;pulls Docker image;&#10;DB lease + attempt&#10;writes; renews lease)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1120" y="1170" width="180" height="120" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_registry" value="Docker Registry" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1130" y="1330" width="160" height="50" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_sched_pollers" value="Scheduled Dispatcher Pollers&#10;(N instances; each owns a&#10;hash partition of job_id;&#10;polls DB every 1s for due jobs;&#10;marks row dispatched;&#10;enqueues to SQS)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="1340" width="240" height="120" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_recur_poller" value="Recurring Job Dispatcher&#10;(polls DB for due recurring&#10;instances; materializes Job&#10;rows; enqueues to SQS)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="1340" width="240" height="120" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c_zk" value="ZooKeeper&#10;(partition ↔ poller&#10;assignment;&#10;failure handover)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="1340" width="180" height="120" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e1" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_client" target="c_lb"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_lb" target="c_jobsvc"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e3" value="write Job /&#10;RecurringJob" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_jobsvc" target="c_db"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e4" value="poll due jobs" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_sched_pollers" target="c_db"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e5" value="enqueue" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_sched_pollers" target="c_sqs"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e6" value="poll + materialize" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_recur_poller" target="c_db"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e7" value="enqueue" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_recur_poller" target="c_sqs"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e8" value="consume" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_workers" target="c_sqs"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e9" value="lease /&#10;attempt /&#10;status" style="endArrow=classic;startArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_workers" target="c_db"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e10" value="pull image" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_workers" target="c_registry"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e11" value="partition assignment" style="endArrow=classic;startArrow=classic;html=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_zk" target="c_sched_pollers"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="30" value="Deep Dives" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#f5f5f5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1500" width="1380" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="31" value="1) At-least-once execution under duplicate SQS delivery&#10;&#10;Problem: SQS is at-least-once. If a worker takes a message and its visibility timeout&#10;expires (slow job, GC pause, network partition) SQS redelivers — two workers can&#10;run the same attempt. Bumping visibility timeout trades duplicate risk for crash&#10;recovery latency; cannot win both.&#10;&#10;Resolution:&#10;  - Atomic DB-row lease on Job (chosen over Redis — durable, no extra component):&#10;      UPDATE jobs&#10;      SET status='running', lease_owner=W, lease_expires=now()+T&#10;      WHERE id=? AND (status='scheduled' OR lease_expires &lt; now())&#10;    Only one worker's update lands; the other drops the message.&#10;  - Worker renews lease while running; if it dies, lease expires and another takes over.&#10;  - Fencing token (monotonic lease epoch) checked on writes to JobExecutionAttempt&#10;    + Job.status — prevents a stale (GC-paused) worker from corrupting state after&#10;    a new owner has taken over." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1530" width="680" height="340" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="32" value="2) Scheduled Dispatcher Poller — scale-out without double dispatch&#10;&#10;Problem: a single poller cannot sustain 10k/s dispatch. Naive scale-out via&#10;LIMIT/OFFSET is broken — concurrent pollers see overlapping rows in the same&#10;snapshot, causing double dispatch.&#10;&#10;Resolution:&#10;  - Hash partition on job_id: poller i of N runs&#10;      WHERE scheduledAt &lt;= now() AND status='scheduled' AND hash(id) % N = i&#10;    Static partitioning, no row overlap, no lock contention.&#10;  - ZooKeeper coordinates partition ↔ poller assignment + handover on failure.&#10;  - Poll every 1s on index (scheduledAt, status) to meet the &lt;3s SLA.&#10;  - Mark row as dispatched (status flip) so the same row is not re-picked on the&#10;    next 1s tick.&#10;&#10;Alternatives considered: SELECT FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED (DB does coordination at&#10;cost of locking overhead); atomic UPDATE ... RETURNING claim." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1530" width="680" height="340" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="33" value="3) Cron storm — 200k jobs scheduled for 9:00:00.000, must fire within 3s&#10;&#10;Problem: 10k concurrent worker cap × 3s SLA cannot run 200k jobs in time, even&#10;if pollers/SQS keep up. The bottleneck is parallel execution capacity.&#10;&#10;Resolution:&#10;  - Smear the storm by adding jitter to scheduledAt at materialization time for&#10;    cron-instance Job rows. Spread the 200k across a window so the worker pool&#10;    is not saturated.&#10;  - Priority levels on RecurringJob control the jitter window:&#10;      high-priority → tight window (small jitter, near the cron time)&#10;      low-priority  → wide window (more spread, looser to SLA)&#10;  - Real schedulers (Airflow, K8s CronJobs) use the same pattern.&#10;&#10;Honest assessment: without jitter, the design does NOT meet the 3s SLA on a&#10;200k storm. Jitter+priority is the standard fix." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1890" width="1380" height="280" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="34" value="4) Cancellation under at-least-once&#10;&#10;Problem: once a message is enqueued in SQS, you cannot selectively delete it.&#10;User calls DELETE /jobs/:id before execution — how does the worker know?&#10;&#10;Resolution: cancel = flip Job.status to 'cancelled' in DB. Worker reads Job&#10;status as part of lease acquisition; if cancelled, drops the SQS message and&#10;does not execute. Cancellation API returns 409 if status is already 'running'&#10;or 'completed'." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2190" width="1380" height="200" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
